{
 "id": "vision_motion_group",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "COMMON MOTION AS THE OBJECT CRITERION. A thing is what moves together (Spelke's cohesion/continuity/contact; common fate before boundary or appearance). Static-form criteria -- enclosure, border ownership -- fragment a scene into however many enclosed regions it contains; common fate should yield FEW and LARGE.\n\nMotion is a VECTOR MATRIX: each MCell carries `v = [vy, vx]` as ONE attribute and every question is a direct `Magnitude(VecSub(..))` read.\n\nThe tolerance falls out of the field's own dispersion (Otsu over the observed adjacent-pair differences); the reference frame falls out as the largest group. No motion-agreement constant appears in this file.\n\nMASTER-OFF by default (PROTOCOL \u00a79): with `marm` at 0.0 no rule fires and every committed result is preserved.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "motion_grouping_visual",
  "definition": "Segmentation by common fate. A proto-object is a maximal connected set of cells whose motion vectors agree within the field's own dispersion, and which moves differently from the scene's dominant motion. Substrate analogue: the substrate's motion-defined proto-object.",
  "category": "vision_domain",
  "parent": "vision_foundation"
 },
 "nodes": [
  {
   "local_id": 0,
   "type": "MotionParams",
   "attrs": {
    "marm": 0.0,
    "mcontrast": 0.0,
    "mtol_exact": 0.0,
    "mflood": 0.0
   }
  }
 ],
