  {
   "name": "mo_mint",
   "comment": "A group is an OBJECT iff it moves DIFFERENTLY FROM THE SCENE'S DOMINANT MOTION, by more than the field's own tolerance -- one direct vector read, `Magnitude(VecSub(R.v, field.dom_v))`, against the SAME self-derived scale that bound the group together. One scale, used to bind and to separate; no second constant is introduced.\n\nTHIS IS THE ARM THAT REFUSES A STABLE BACKGROUND PATCH. A patch of wall is part of the dominant group (or moves with it), so its contrast is zero and it is refused however beautifully it persists. A global camera pan is refused by the same test: the whole field is the dominant group, and nothing differs from it.\n\n`mcontrast` DISARMS the contrast test and is the DEAD-INSTRUMENT control: with it off, a uniformly translating field mints ONE object covering every cell -- a field containing no figure at all. It is graph DATA, so the control is the agent's own configuration, not a fork in the host (PROTOCOL \u00a70).",
